Usage: xxd [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Make a hexdump or do the reverse.

OPTIONS:
  -r, --reverse     reverse: convert hex to binary
  -p, --plain       plain hexdump
  -c, --cols NUM    set bytes per line
  -l, --len NUM     limit input to LEN bytes
  -s, --seek NUM    start at SEEK bytes into input
  -o, --offset NUM  add OFFSET to displayed file position
  -u, --upper-case  use upper-case hex digits
  -g, --group NUM   set bytes per hex group
  -i, --include     output in C include file style
  -n, --name ARG    set the variable name used in C include output
      --help        display this help and exit
  -V, --version     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
